cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "(D, δ): a two-feature signature for memory-access traces"
abstract: >-
  A low-cost, calibration-free signature for memory-access traces of a logical array:
  relative access density (D), information-equivalent to a normalized access count, and
  index-trajectory drift (delta), the net direction of the access trajectory over time.
  The pair flags O(n log n) to O(n^2) degradation of the same code without per-class
  calibration. The repository provides TypeScript and Python implementations that
  reproduce all results bit for bit, a deterministic corpus of seven sorting algorithms
  across five problem sizes and three input patterns, a pre-registered cross-domain
  validation on four non-sorting workloads, and a robustness analysis of the drift
  feature.
